&lt;p&gt;As an Intermediate Backend Engineer, you will take backend features and improvements from clarifying the problem through shipping them and following up in production. You will work within a product area, partnering with Product Management, Frontend, Infrastructure, and Security to deliver predictably and contribute to the quality, security, performance, and maintainability of shared backend code and services. You will be trusted to work with minimal guidance, to know when to seek help, and to communicate clearly in a remote, asynchronous environment — with other tenured engineers alongside you to review your work, think through hard problems with you, and help you grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why you’ll love this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll take features from requirements through delivery and follow-up; your code will run on a platform used by millions of users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning and Growth :&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll work alongside your engineering team, who treat code review and design review as a learning loop rather than a gate — one of the fastest ways to grow your engineering judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovative Culture:&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll use AI as a genuine part of daily engineering work, developing the judgment to know when to trust it and when not to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Autonomy:&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll thrive in our remote-first, asynchronous organization, where clear written communication and self-direction are the pillars of success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;User-Centric Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll partner closely with PMs and designers to shape requirements, so you understand why you’re building something, not just what.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own and Ship Features:&lt;/strong&gt; Design, implement, test, and ship backend features and improvements with minimal guidance, working in Ruby/Rails, Go, or any other modern languages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build for Production:&lt;/strong&gt; Write maintainable, secure, observable, and performant code. Design and maintain APIs, background jobs, integrations, and bounded service functionality, and work with data models, migrations, indexes, and query behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
